From 7c0a3eb9d73c5a131428de362a16b88fd6d68ab2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <virajslko@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:13:43 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] filesystem: find an asset whose name differs only in
 case

Wallpaper Engine runs on Windows, whose filesystem ignores case, so
Workshop scenes reference their files in whatever case the author typed:
a model naming materials/shadow.json while its scene.pkg holds
materials/Shadow.json loads in Wallpaper Engine and failed here
(AssetLocator::readString threw, the project load returned NULL).

When no mountpoint has the exact path, Container now asks each adapter, in
mount order, for a file matching it ignoring ASCII case
(Adapter::findIgnoringCase: the package's file list; a directory walked one
component at a time, staying inside its base path) and opens that one,
logging "Found <requested> as <actual> (case differs)". Every mountpoint is
tried exactly first, so an exact match anywhere still wins and lookups that
hit pay nothing; only a miss costs a scan.

Origin: ours
Why: Workshop scenes with a case-mismatched asset reference failed to load in lp-player's scene worker (scene corpus: 3354740764)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
